From: cyclic-dma-fix
Subject: [PATCH] jupiter_sdr: make RX1 byte DMA cyclic (CYCLIC 0 -> 1)

Root cause of the ~2%/1-frame-per-transfer-boundary RX loss: axi_adrv9001_rx1_dma
is synthesized with CONFIG.CYCLIC 0, so after every K-packet S2MM transfer the
host must reset+resubmit the single engine. A late resubmit misses the next
frame's SYNC_TRANSFER_START tuser -> ~1 lost frame per transfer boundary.
CYCLIC 1 lets the engine auto-restart in hardware (single-cycle re-arm) so the
host round-trip is removed from the frame-boundary re-arm path.

Target file (relative to repo root):
  jupiter_byte_lean_build/hdl_prj_jupiter_composite/vivado_ip_prj/projects/jupiter_sdr/system_bd.tcl

Verified against the actual file: the ONLY line that changes is line 325
(rx1). Line 326 (SYNC_TRANSFER_START 1) is intentionally left unchanged --
see the note on rx2 and SYNC below.

--- a/jupiter_byte_lean_build/hdl_prj_jupiter_composite/vivado_ip_prj/projects/jupiter_sdr/system_bd.tcl
+++ b/jupiter_byte_lean_build/hdl_prj_jupiter_composite/vivado_ip_prj/projects/jupiter_sdr/system_bd.tcl
@@ -322,7 +322,7 @@ ad_ip_instance axi_dmac axi_adrv9001_rx1_dma
 ad_ip_instance axi_dmac axi_adrv9001_rx1_dma
 ad_ip_parameter axi_adrv9001_rx1_dma CONFIG.DMA_TYPE_SRC 2
 ad_ip_parameter axi_adrv9001_rx1_dma CONFIG.DMA_TYPE_DEST 0
-ad_ip_parameter axi_adrv9001_rx1_dma CONFIG.CYCLIC 0
+ad_ip_parameter axi_adrv9001_rx1_dma CONFIG.CYCLIC 1
 ad_ip_parameter axi_adrv9001_rx1_dma CONFIG.SYNC_TRANSFER_START 1
 ad_ip_parameter axi_adrv9001_rx1_dma CONFIG.AXI_SLICE_SRC 0
 ad_ip_parameter axi_adrv9001_rx1_dma CONFIG.AXI_SLICE_DEST 0

================================================================================
NOTES (grounded in the IP source under vivado_ip_prj/library/axi_dmac/)
================================================================================

rx2 (line 345, CONFIG.CYCLIC 0):
  RX2 is NOT consumed by the byte link (the host only opens/arms rxd = rx1;
  see host_app_k5/qpsk_tun.c:587 `static struct dmac rxd;` and the single RX
  path). Leaving rx2 at CYCLIC 0 is the minimal, lowest-risk change and does
  not affect the byte link. If a future consumer wants symmetric behaviour,
  apply the identical 0->1 edit to line 345; it is otherwise unnecessary.

SYNC_TRANSFER_START (unchanged, stays 1):
  request_sync_transfer_start is a pure synthesis tie (regmap_request.v:161:
  `assign request_sync_transfer_start = SYNC_TRANSFER_START ? 1'b1 : 1'b0;`).
  It still gates the START of each (now hardware-auto-restarted) cyclic lap on
  the frame `req_sync` tuser, which is exactly what keeps the ring base aligned
  to a frame boundary. Keep it at 1.

CONFIG.CYCLIC 1 is PERMISSIVE, not mandatory, at the register level:
  regmap_request.v:188  `up_dma_cyclic <= up_wdata[0] & DMA_CYCLIC;`
  The per-transfer cyclic bit (FLAGS reg 0x40C bit0) is AND-gated by the
  DMA_CYCLIC synthesis parameter. A CYCLIC-1 bitstream therefore still runs the
  CURRENT (non-cyclic) host binary unchanged, because the host writes FLAGS=0
  today (qpsk_tun.c:624). Cyclic behaviour is only engaged when the host also
  sets FLAGS bit0. This makes the bitstream swap a safe rollout rather than a
  flag-day: deploy the CYCLIC-1 image first, verify the legacy host still works,
  then switch the host to the cyclic path (env-gated, see HOST_RING_REWRITE.md).
